cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
title: FissionFragmentsDomain.jl
abstract: >-
  The fragments of binary fission as models of prompt emission and of the excitation-energy
  partition see them: fissioning systems, the atomic mass evaluation, the isobaric charge
  distribution and the fragmentation domain built from it, fragment level density parameters,
  the energy balance, the relation between the temperature ratio of a fragment pair and the
  division of its excitation energy, fragment yields and averages over them, and the run record
  through which a temperature-ratio extraction hands its curves to a consumer.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gogîță
    given-names: Paul-Adrian
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/FissionFragmentsDomain.jl
keywords:
  - nuclear fission
  - fission fragments
  - isobaric charge distribution
  - level density
  - excitation energy partition
  - temperature ratio
  - Julia
